WEBVTT

00:00:01.920 --> 00:00:03.170
Move, Reiko!

00:00:03.170 --> 00:00:04.850
I'm sitting here!

00:00:05.140 --> 00:00:10.090
B-but didn't you say we could take turns after ten swings?

00:00:10.090 --> 00:00:11.390
I'm changing the rules!

00:00:12.250 --> 00:00:15.420
You get to play with Reishiro all the time.

00:00:15.760 --> 00:00:18.260
I get to be with Reishiro today!

00:00:21.140 --> 00:00:22.490
Kids!

00:00:23.020 --> 00:00:24.750
Your tea is ready.

00:00:25.230 --> 00:00:27.250
Oh, boy! Snack time!

00:00:28.350 --> 00:00:30.270
Come on, Reishiro, Reiko.

00:00:32.440 --> 00:00:34.220
I'm first!

00:00:36.040 --> 00:00:37.000
Oh, my.

00:00:37.240 --> 00:00:38.590
My baby girl.

00:00:38.590 --> 00:00:39.650
Mommy.

00:00:39.650 --> 00:00:40.940
You smell nice.

00:00:49.360 --> 00:00:57.530
<i>Asura Cryin'</i>

00:02:10.940 --> 00:02:15.150
"Together in the Ordinary and Extraordinary"

00:02:21.060 --> 00:02:24.280
Kanade, make a stuffed chamois next!

00:02:26.010 --> 00:02:27.260
Kanade...

00:02:27.260 --> 00:02:28.410
...what do I do here?

00:02:28.410 --> 00:02:30.410
Oh, you saddle stitch.

00:02:32.110 --> 00:02:33.460
Ouch!

00:02:33.750 --> 00:02:36.580
An, you don't know how to sew.

00:02:36.730 --> 00:02:40.280
That's why I'm having Kanade teach me.

00:02:40.760 --> 00:02:42.970
What are you making, anyway?

00:02:43.650 --> 00:02:45.190
A traffic safety good luck charm.

00:02:45.190 --> 00:02:46.340
That's huge!

00:02:46.580 --> 00:02:48.340
Are you going somewhere, An?

00:02:48.340 --> 00:02:52.400
Not me. The upperclassmen of the track team are going on a trip.

00:02:52.400 --> 00:02:53.640
A trip?

00:02:53.640 --> 00:02:59.600
Yeah. Starting next week, all the sophomores are going on a school trip.

00:03:00.130 --> 00:03:01.380
The sophomores?

00:03:01.380 --> 00:03:02.920
That's Shuri's class.

00:03:02.920 --> 00:03:05.520
An, do you know where they're going?

00:03:05.900 --> 00:03:07.630
Hawaii.

00:03:07.660 --> 00:03:09.660
"Class 2-4"

00:03:10.180 --> 00:03:14.550
I should be okay with this man shotgun shells and missiles.

00:03:14.980 --> 00:03:19.210
I wonder if I'll need a jet pack and a Gatling gun?

00:03:19.210 --> 00:03:20.460
Shuri Kurosaki.

00:03:20.940 --> 00:03:22.910
Don't get too excited.

00:03:23.640 --> 00:03:25.610
Look who's talking.

00:03:25.940 --> 00:03:29.020
You look out of place.

00:03:29.550 --> 00:03:31.760
These shirts are the formal dress of Hawaii.

00:03:32.430 --> 00:03:34.690
I wish I were going on a school trip.

00:03:34.930 --> 00:03:37.430
I'd love to go to Hawaii.

00:03:37.720 --> 00:03:38.630
Oh, yeah.

00:03:38.630 --> 00:03:40.550
You were held back a grade.

00:03:42.240 --> 00:03:43.490
Sucks to be stupid.

00:03:47.040 --> 00:03:52.140
I think Shuri mentioned something about doing a swimsuit fashion show tonight.

00:03:52.140 --> 00:03:53.430
I'm going!

00:03:53.430 --> 00:03:54.110
What?

00:03:54.540 --> 00:03:56.650
It's a waste for you to be the only one to worship it!

00:03:56.800 --> 00:03:59.680
Kurosaki-senpai's amazing figure...

00:03:59.680 --> 00:04:01.680
...is the treasure of Rakurowa High School!

00:04:03.290 --> 00:04:04.870
You really think so?

00:04:04.870 --> 00:04:06.170
She looks terrible in the morning.

00:04:06.890 --> 00:04:09.630
She sits cross-legged in just a shirt with bed head.

00:04:10.020 --> 00:04:11.790
Cross-legged with just a shirt?

00:04:15.450 --> 00:04:18.040
What are you, Tomo?

00:04:18.520 --> 00:04:22.030
You get to flirt with the cute Misao all day long...

00:04:22.030 --> 00:04:25.250
...and live with the hottest girl at school!

00:04:25.780 --> 00:04:26.600
Is that it?

00:04:26.840 --> 00:04:29.190
Are you the protagonist of some anime?

00:04:29.340 --> 00:04:31.190
Look, uh, Higuchi...

00:04:31.190 --> 00:04:32.370
Tomoharu Natsume.

00:04:33.230 --> 00:04:35.970
What did you do this time?

00:04:35.970 --> 00:04:38.080
What are you talking about, Saeki?

00:04:38.370 --> 00:04:39.090
I said...

00:04:41.020 --> 00:04:42.940
S-sorry, Takatsuki!

00:04:44.240 --> 00:04:45.390
Reiko?

00:04:45.390 --> 00:04:47.840
S-sorry! Are you okay?

00:04:48.950 --> 00:04:51.010
I hurt my ankle.

00:04:51.400 --> 00:04:52.310
Huh?

00:04:58.660 --> 00:05:00.050
How's your ankle?

00:05:00.290 --> 00:05:01.150
It's fine.

00:05:01.150 --> 00:05:02.550
It's just a little sprained.

00:05:02.550 --> 00:05:04.710
I could have gone home myself.

00:05:05.770 --> 00:05:06.870
I see.

00:05:09.610 --> 00:05:11.780
Say something.

00:05:12.550 --> 00:05:14.080
What do you mean?

00:05:14.080 --> 00:05:15.620
Anything.

00:05:15.620 --> 00:05:18.600
You don't think it's awkward to sit in silence?

00:05:18.790 --> 00:05:20.600
Huh? Oh, uh...

00:05:21.970 --> 00:05:23.220
Oh, I know!

00:05:23.220 --> 00:05:26.870
The other day, Higuchi found some kishimen on the ground...

00:05:23.220 --> 00:05:26.870
(Kishimen: flat udon)

00:05:26.530 --> 00:05:28.870
I don't want to hear about Higuchi's antics.

00:05:28.870 --> 00:05:30.040
Oh?

00:05:30.040 --> 00:05:30.950
Then...

00:05:33.980 --> 00:05:34.610
What?

00:05:34.890 --> 00:05:36.530
Nothing. Your hair...

00:05:38.110 --> 00:05:39.990
It gets in the way, so I tied it.

00:05:40.610 --> 00:05:41.770
That ribbon.

00:05:42.250 --> 00:05:44.460
I like its classic look.

00:05:44.800 --> 00:05:45.710
And besides...

00:05:46.330 --> 00:05:48.210
...it looks good on you.

00:05:49.070 --> 00:05:51.810
What are you saying? Don't be stupid.

00:05:52.920 --> 00:05:56.140
Cut it out, Saeki! Ow!

00:05:57.000 --> 00:05:57.920
What's going on?

00:05:58.060 --> 00:05:58.830
Nothing!

00:06:02.100 --> 00:06:05.750
It's the matching ribbon my aunt bought me.

00:06:06.180 --> 00:06:07.050
Matching?

00:06:07.050 --> 00:06:08.920
You don't mean your brother...

00:06:08.920 --> 00:06:09.840
With Aine.

00:06:20.410 --> 00:06:21.080
Saeki!

00:06:29.880 --> 00:06:31.850
Reishiro, this is just...

00:06:31.850 --> 00:06:34.780
We weren't doing anything weird!

00:06:34.780 --> 00:06:39.540
I hurt Saeki, so I was helping her home.

00:06:41.320 --> 00:06:42.810
You spilled the beans.

00:06:42.810 --> 00:06:44.150
This is perfect.

00:06:44.490 --> 00:06:46.750
Tomoharu Natsume, Misao Minakami.

00:06:47.040 --> 00:06:49.580
I'd like to invite you to a party.

00:06:49.870 --> 00:06:50.740
Huh?

00:06:58.910 --> 00:07:01.020
What are we doing here?

00:07:01.020 --> 00:07:05.970
Can you imagine what he would have done if we refused?

00:07:06.120 --> 00:07:09.480
Grow a pair, Tomoharu Natsume.

00:07:09.820 --> 00:07:12.220
What are all of you doing here?

00:07:12.370 --> 00:07:17.030
We get a prize for doing a short performance.

00:07:17.220 --> 00:07:21.210
How can I pass up an opportunity like that?

00:07:21.450 --> 00:07:24.280
We're not doing so well financially.

00:07:24.570 --> 00:07:26.930
I'll sell that prize for some cash.

00:07:26.930 --> 00:07:29.810
Don't count your chickens.

00:07:29.810 --> 00:07:32.170
Did you say something, Shuri Kurosaki?

00:07:32.550 --> 00:07:37.500
Nia, feel free to take all their luck today.

00:07:37.690 --> 00:07:39.910
I don't need their disgusting luck.

00:07:40.240 --> 00:07:41.640
Right, Kanade?

00:07:44.660 --> 00:07:47.310
Are you also here for the prize, Susugihara?

00:07:48.120 --> 00:07:53.460
There's a rare species of rose growing in the gardens here.

00:07:53.800 --> 00:07:54.710
I'm here to see those.

00:07:55.000 --> 00:07:56.150
Just for that?

00:07:56.530 --> 00:07:59.080
Yes. Care to join me?

00:07:59.470 --> 00:08:01.000
I'd rather die.

00:08:01.200 --> 00:08:02.450
Too bad.

00:08:02.640 --> 00:08:05.190
I guess I'll have to invite you in the afterlife.

00:08:09.370 --> 00:08:11.770
They're like an unhappy couple.

00:08:16.000 --> 00:08:17.920
Thank you for waiting.

00:08:19.030 --> 00:08:22.200
Reiko, that's an unusual look for you.

00:08:22.920 --> 00:08:25.710
I thought I'd change it up.

00:08:25.710 --> 00:08:28.260
It's not because of something someone said.

00:08:34.310 --> 00:08:35.130
What?

00:08:35.130 --> 00:08:36.470
Nothing.

00:08:38.730 --> 00:08:40.180
Reiko.

00:08:40.560 --> 00:08:42.180
Your ribbon is coming undone.

00:08:45.410 --> 00:08:46.950
Thank you.

00:08:56.040 --> 00:08:56.900
That's right.

00:08:56.900 --> 00:08:58.630
Saeki can't see her.

00:09:03.920 --> 00:09:04.690
Tada!

00:09:05.220 --> 00:09:08.100
Welcome, everyone!

00:09:10.890 --> 00:09:11.900
How tacky.

00:09:13.960 --> 00:09:15.740
This is my aunt Kirie Shizuma.

00:09:15.740 --> 00:09:17.040
Nice to meet you.

00:09:17.570 --> 00:09:19.390
You must be Tomoharu and Misao.

00:09:19.390 --> 00:09:20.310
I wanted to meet you.

00:09:20.690 --> 00:09:21.460
Huh?

00:09:22.610 --> 00:09:26.410
I can't believe how many people showed up.

00:09:26.940 --> 00:09:28.050
Thank you, Reishiro.

00:09:28.290 --> 00:09:29.630
N-not at all.

00:09:30.540 --> 00:09:33.720
I'll go get more food.

00:09:36.700 --> 00:09:38.190
I'm sure Aine would be happy.

00:09:38.570 --> 00:09:40.880
Let's make this a great party.

00:09:41.790 --> 00:09:42.880
Aine?

00:09:44.920 --> 00:09:47.510
Yes. She's Aine's mother.

00:09:48.140 --> 00:09:49.510
Her?

00:09:49.510 --> 00:09:51.840
You didn't know, Tomoharu Natsume?

00:09:52.610 --> 00:09:55.250
Well, but...

00:09:55.250 --> 00:09:57.250
...their personalities are totally different.

00:09:58.950 --> 00:10:01.790
How is this Aine's party?

00:10:04.090 --> 00:10:06.020
Today is the anniversary of her death.

00:10:16.350 --> 00:10:20.910
You mean the day she became a burial doll?

00:10:24.520 --> 00:10:27.640
My aunt didn't want a somber event...

00:10:28.170 --> 00:10:30.480
...so she's hosting this party.

00:10:39.660 --> 00:10:42.590
Oh, Misao. Give me a few minutes.

00:10:43.120 --> 00:10:44.660
I just have to arrange it.

00:10:44.660 --> 00:10:47.200
Wow! This looks delicious!

00:10:48.120 --> 00:10:50.670
I teach at a culinary school.

00:10:51.430 --> 00:10:54.410
Why don't you come by for some lessons?

00:10:55.470 --> 00:10:58.400
But I can't touch anything.

00:11:00.570 --> 00:11:01.720
It doesn't matter.

00:11:01.720 --> 00:11:04.840
You can learn the recipes and teach them to Tomoharu.

00:11:05.660 --> 00:11:06.480
Teach Tomo?

00:11:06.480 --> 00:11:08.640
Well, Reishiro can do it.

00:11:08.930 --> 00:11:11.380
That guy can cook?

00:11:11.910 --> 00:11:14.650
Yes! Reishiro cooks.

00:11:17.580 --> 00:11:21.090
I can't picture someone with such a sour expression making anything good.

00:11:21.570 --> 00:11:24.020
He doesn't laugh at school either?

00:11:25.080 --> 00:11:27.430
He used to be full of smiles.

00:11:28.300 --> 00:11:30.320
He was so kind to Aine and Reiko.

00:11:31.040 --> 00:11:32.190
Maybe it's a phase.

00:11:33.250 --> 00:11:35.840
What was Aine like?

00:11:36.520 --> 00:11:39.300
She was outgoing, mischievous, and hated to lose.

00:11:39.590 --> 00:11:41.370
She made Reiko cry a lot.

00:11:41.370 --> 00:11:42.520
Reiko?

00:11:42.520 --> 00:11:45.550
Yes. They were always fighting over Reishiro.

00:11:45.790 --> 00:11:50.550
But I haven't seen Reiko cry at all in the last year.

00:11:51.370 --> 00:11:53.960
A girl can change a lot in a year.

00:11:55.500 --> 00:11:56.460
You're right.

00:12:04.490 --> 00:12:05.740
Testing.

00:12:05.880 --> 00:12:09.820
Let the short performance contest begin!

00:12:12.280 --> 00:12:14.340
Why is Mahiwa the emcee?

00:12:14.340 --> 00:12:16.220
Mrs. Kirie chose him.

00:12:16.460 --> 00:12:19.970
She found the lowest ranking one among us.

00:12:20.350 --> 00:12:22.800
First up is President Rikka!

00:12:25.590 --> 00:12:26.650
Tomoharu Natsume.

00:12:27.170 --> 00:12:28.650
Give me a 10,000 yen bill.

00:12:28.650 --> 00:12:30.110
Huh? Sure.

00:12:32.320 --> 00:12:34.530
Pay attention, ladies and gentlemen.

00:12:34.860 --> 00:12:37.510
I place this handkerchief over the bill...

00:12:39.240 --> 00:12:41.590
The 10,000 yen turned into 500 yen!

00:12:42.360 --> 00:12:44.240
There you have it.

00:12:44.530 --> 00:12:46.240
Amazing, Rikka!

00:12:46.400 --> 00:12:47.750
Hey, President Rikka.

00:12:48.420 --> 00:12:50.770
Give me back my 10,000 yen.

00:12:50.770 --> 00:12:51.970
He noticed.

00:12:53.800 --> 00:12:55.630
This is a 1,000 yen bill!

00:12:56.400 --> 00:12:58.660
Next up are Kurosaki and Ania!

00:13:01.920 --> 00:13:02.840
What are they doing?

00:13:02.840 --> 00:13:03.510
I don't know.

00:13:05.720 --> 00:13:06.780
Kurosaki!

00:13:07.160 --> 00:13:08.270
Run!

00:13:13.460 --> 00:13:14.230
Well?

00:13:14.230 --> 00:13:17.690
I took the missiles' luck and controlled their explosions.

00:13:18.020 --> 00:13:19.610
I see.

00:13:19.610 --> 00:13:21.000
What an idea.

00:13:21.000 --> 00:13:23.170
Amazing! How thrilling!

00:13:23.460 --> 00:13:25.670
It was our pleasure.

00:13:27.200 --> 00:13:30.670
You put a lot of thought into your performance.

00:13:31.000 --> 00:13:32.880
You're cute as always, Shuri.

00:13:34.850 --> 00:13:35.860
You moron, Shuri!

00:13:35.860 --> 00:13:37.680
I didn't take luck from those!

00:13:47.200 --> 00:13:49.410
That was my performance, madam.

00:13:53.640 --> 00:13:54.550
Vivian?

00:13:54.840 --> 00:13:55.990
Go, Vivian.

00:14:03.160 --> 00:14:04.840
Ring of fire, success!

00:14:06.280 --> 00:14:08.590
Next is Kanade.

00:14:08.920 --> 00:14:10.800
Oh, um...

00:14:11.330 --> 00:14:13.250
They're ordinary words...

00:14:13.250 --> 00:14:16.420
...but there's something strange about them.

00:14:16.710 --> 00:14:20.120
Shuttlecock, pussyfoot, wood...

00:14:19.740 --> 00:14:21.320
Wait a second, Takatsuki.

00:14:21.470 --> 00:14:23.100
Something's fishy.

00:14:24.250 --> 00:14:27.190
Woodpecker and titmouse?

00:14:27.190 --> 00:14:28.150
Tit...!

00:14:29.400 --> 00:14:31.700
What's so weird about these words?

00:14:32.040 --> 00:14:35.650
Shuri wrote this for me.

00:14:35.210 --> 00:14:35.930
Shuri!

00:14:36.320 --> 00:14:38.720
What? Is there a problem?

00:14:40.500 --> 00:14:42.420
Uh, okay...

00:14:42.420 --> 00:14:43.620
Here we go.

00:14:46.600 --> 00:14:49.440
Out of body experience!

00:14:51.030 --> 00:14:52.080
And...

00:14:53.520 --> 00:14:55.500
In body experience.

00:14:58.430 --> 00:15:02.080
Your courage is admirable, Tomoharu Natsume.

00:15:06.550 --> 00:15:09.960
Auntie, you don't have to laugh.

00:15:10.540 --> 00:15:11.790
Oh, no.

00:15:11.790 --> 00:15:14.140
Thinking about how Aine would have enjoyed it...

00:15:14.140 --> 00:15:15.970
...made it funny for some reason.

00:15:16.400 --> 00:15:20.490
She also had a lot of flops trying to make people laugh.

00:15:31.010 --> 00:15:32.260
It's Darjeeling tea.

00:15:32.260 --> 00:15:33.180
Thank you.

00:15:39.860 --> 00:15:41.010
Reishiro.

00:15:42.930 --> 00:15:45.530
You don't laugh enough.

00:15:45.530 --> 00:15:48.120
Your face is stiff.

00:15:48.120 --> 00:15:49.370
Auntie.

00:15:50.580 --> 00:15:53.410
Don't worry about it, Reishiro.

00:15:53.800 --> 00:15:56.820
I loved it when you smiled.

00:15:57.350 --> 00:15:58.020
Of course.

00:16:00.040 --> 00:16:00.760
Come in.

00:16:01.730 --> 00:16:02.760
Excuse us.

00:16:02.760 --> 00:16:03.360
Oh!

00:16:03.790 --> 00:16:05.570
I'll be leaving, then.

00:16:07.450 --> 00:16:09.270
We were wondering about the results.

00:16:09.850 --> 00:16:11.000
How is it looking?

00:16:11.190 --> 00:16:12.780
I can't say. It's still a secret.

00:16:13.210 --> 00:16:15.280
Too bad.

00:16:16.340 --> 00:16:18.600
You're so much like Aine.

00:16:26.090 --> 00:16:28.110
You really are a ghost.

00:16:29.990 --> 00:16:31.720
I can't see her...

00:16:31.960 --> 00:16:34.310
...but Aine is with Reishiro, isn't she?

00:16:34.600 --> 00:16:36.040
Just like you.

00:16:36.430 --> 00:16:37.530
Yes.

00:16:37.960 --> 00:16:39.840
I see. That's good.

00:16:40.700 --> 00:16:43.010
Aine must be happy.

00:16:43.590 --> 00:16:46.900
She always loved Reishiro.

00:16:47.390 --> 00:16:49.500
She must be happy to be with him.

00:16:50.460 --> 00:16:51.230
Of course.

00:16:52.000 --> 00:16:52.860
Thank you.

00:16:53.630 --> 00:16:56.610
For some reason, I can believe what you say.

00:17:01.130 --> 00:17:02.000
Mommy.

00:17:14.730 --> 00:17:16.320
The results are in.

00:17:16.800 --> 00:17:17.570
Really.

00:17:18.770 --> 00:17:19.830
Saeki?

00:17:20.790 --> 00:17:21.510
Natsume.

00:17:22.090 --> 00:17:24.540
Thank you for coming to see my aunt.

00:17:24.540 --> 00:17:27.470
Oh, it was nothing.

00:17:32.320 --> 00:17:34.050
Sometimes I wonder.

00:17:34.730 --> 00:17:37.990
Maybe the one trapped inside the Asura Machina...

00:17:38.570 --> 00:17:41.840
...was me, not Aine.

00:17:42.700 --> 00:17:46.310
I know my brother suffers...

00:17:47.080 --> 00:17:48.910
...and I'm lonely.

00:17:49.390 --> 00:17:54.480
But I'm slightly relieved not to have been in Aine's position.

00:17:54.720 --> 00:17:55.920
I know it's pathetic.

00:17:56.400 --> 00:17:58.850
I wouldn't say that.

00:18:00.300 --> 00:18:01.060
Yeah.

00:18:01.550 --> 00:18:04.040
No one's more pathetic than Tomo.

00:18:04.240 --> 00:18:06.110
He gets sick before his exams.

00:18:06.450 --> 00:18:08.610
He gets bossed around by a little girl.

00:18:08.610 --> 00:18:10.100
And he has perverted dreams.

00:18:11.060 --> 00:18:14.230
How would you know what I dream about?

00:18:14.470 --> 00:18:17.360
I possessed you while you were asleep and took a look inside your head.

00:18:17.360 --> 00:18:18.320
Yeah, right!

00:18:19.670 --> 00:18:20.530
Saeki?

00:18:20.630 --> 00:18:22.690
Are you two always like this?

00:18:23.510 --> 00:18:24.810
Yup! Just like this.

00:18:25.190 --> 00:18:27.360
Ghosts aren't so bad, right?

00:18:34.080 --> 00:18:35.670
That's the prize?

00:18:36.150 --> 00:18:37.500
Seems kind of small.

00:18:37.740 --> 00:18:40.570
Whatever. It'll just make it easier to find a buyer.

00:18:40.910 --> 00:18:42.980
I'd like to announce the results.

00:18:43.310 --> 00:18:44.220
The winner is...

00:18:46.920 --> 00:18:48.650
Tomoharu and Misao!

00:18:48.650 --> 00:18:49.320
Huh?

00:18:49.560 --> 00:18:51.320
What?

00:18:51.320 --> 00:18:51.770
Really?

00:18:52.490 --> 00:18:53.400
Hooray!

00:18:54.030 --> 00:18:56.870
See, Tomo? Aren't you glad we did that?

00:18:57.200 --> 00:19:00.130
For the winners, we have...

00:18:59.700 --> 00:19:00.900
Wait a minute!

00:19:01.430 --> 00:19:02.780
I can't accept this.

00:19:02.780 --> 00:19:04.270
Why Tomoharu Natsume?

00:19:04.560 --> 00:19:07.970
I felt bad for their weak performance.

00:19:08.450 --> 00:19:10.900
I guess this is more of a consolation prize.

00:19:11.520 --> 00:19:12.580
So it's come to this.

00:19:15.270 --> 00:19:16.670
The prize is mine!

00:19:16.960 --> 00:19:19.700
President, now you're just a villain!

00:19:19.940 --> 00:19:21.140
Shut up, Mahiwa!

00:19:21.620 --> 00:19:25.320
If you want it, come and get it, Tomoharu Natsume.

00:19:30.650 --> 00:19:32.380
This just gets worse and worse.

00:19:32.670 --> 00:19:33.780
Ew!

00:19:37.330 --> 00:19:39.880
Where did you get this?

00:19:40.170 --> 00:19:42.280
I won it in an online auction!

00:19:42.810 --> 00:19:45.700
Don't you think it would make a good fertility charm?

00:19:49.450 --> 00:19:51.610
Tomoharu Natsume, Misao Minakami.

00:19:52.330 --> 00:19:55.020
Sorry for putting you through that nonsense.

00:19:55.360 --> 00:19:57.570
No one thought it was nonsense.

00:19:59.590 --> 00:20:00.740
Sheesh.

00:20:01.030 --> 00:20:03.290
What a worthless day.

00:20:03.670 --> 00:20:06.170
What a waste.

00:20:07.280 --> 00:20:09.010
What a wonderful aunt.

00:20:09.390 --> 00:20:11.940
I wouldn't mind being loved by her.

00:20:12.950 --> 00:20:15.020
See you at home, Tomoharu.

00:20:15.210 --> 00:20:17.180
Thanks for the fun.

00:20:27.940 --> 00:20:28.810
Misao.

00:20:29.530 --> 00:20:33.040
You were just making up how Aine felt, weren't you?

00:20:34.380 --> 00:20:35.780
Not really.

00:20:36.070 --> 00:20:37.120
I just know.

00:20:37.120 --> 00:20:38.810
What do you mean?

00:20:42.460 --> 00:20:44.140
I just do.

00:20:51.880 --> 00:20:53.030
They all left.

00:20:56.350 --> 00:20:58.610
Sit with me, Reishiro.

00:20:59.420 --> 00:21:00.910
Just sit.

00:21:11.100 --> 00:21:14.040
I'll let Aine sit next to you today.

00:21:14.760 --> 00:21:15.570
Reiko.

00:21:16.730 --> 00:21:18.940
Your tea is ready!

00:21:19.370 --> 00:21:23.070
Let's talk about the party so we can make it better next year!

00:21:23.700 --> 00:21:24.800
Coming!

00:21:33.020 --> 00:21:34.030
Reishiro!

00:21:34.030 --> 00:21:35.140
Come on!

00:21:43.110 --> 00:21:44.600
Let's go, Aine.

00:23:19.960 --> 00:23:25.150
"Preview"

00:23:20.970 --> 00:23:23.280
Time is running out.

00:23:23.280 --> 00:23:24.090
Wait.

00:23:24.330 --> 00:23:25.340
Rustling.

00:23:25.730 --> 00:23:26.590
Hand it over.

00:23:26.930 --> 00:23:27.700
Disappointing.

00:23:27.840 --> 00:23:28.750
But that's okay.

00:23:28.950 --> 00:23:31.160
Sending the scream of the soul.

00:23:31.500 --> 00:23:35.010
"Until the End of the World"
